Patch summary:
Android 17 desktop-windowing fixes, ported to Android 16 QPR2's WM Shell:
- eb4e95ba6: re-lay out desk tasks when the display size changes at the same
  density (a host window resize), not only when the density changes. Android
  16 sends no display-change transition for such a resize, which the handler
  waited for, so the stable insets of the new size trigger the re-layout.
- 31c539246: bring an active but empty desk to the front when a desktop task
  opens in it, so the task is not left invisible behind the desktop wallpaper
  activity or Home.
- dd40361930: FreeformFallbackTransitionObserver moves freeform tasks that
  launched outside any desk into the display's default desk, activating it if
  needed, with a holding transition that keeps them visible. It uses Android
  16's desk creation in DesktopTasksController, and skips displays without a
  desktop (Ika's app-window displays).
- f81f04d0b and bde4b0aee: when the desktop wallpaper goes to back, the desk
  stays active if a task in it went full-immersive, and stays active in the
  repository when the keyguard appears so that unlocking returns to it.
- db552a3d6, in part: a recents transition deactivates the desk on the desk's
  own display instead of the default display. The delay until Overview hides
  needs Overview-visibility tracking that Android 16's Shell does not have.

